{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/90547?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/90547?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/90547?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/90547?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/90547?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/90547?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A90547"}, "created": "1974-09-01T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-06T13:54:57.174395+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "87", "page_end": "188", "year": 1975, "page_start": "176", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "DeTar, Carleton E."}, {"full_name": "Ellis, S.D."}, {"full_name": "Landshoff, P.V."}], "texkeys": ["DeTar:1974vx"], "imprints": [{"date": "1975"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "It is shown that, in standard parton models, initial and final state interactions do not contribute to the leading asymptotic behaviour of the single particle inclusive cross section for the production of a large p T lepton or hadron in hadron-hadron collisions. However, they do have an important effect on the distribution of accompanying small p T hadrons: superimposed on the large p T event is a \u201cpionization\u201d distribution characteristic of ordinary hadron-hadron collisions. Thus, for example, the cross section for massive lepton pair production is given simply by the Drell-Yan term, though this does not by itself describe the accompanying final state hadrons."}], "control_number": 90547, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(75)90260-6"}], "titles": [{"title": "Final State Interactions in Large Transverse Momentum Lepton and Hadron Production"}], "author_count": 3, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "90547"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mos